@MoLow Neither @nodejs/loaders nor @nodejs/modules were tagged on this PR so I’m just now learning about it. The new `--test-reporter` flag and `requireOrImport` function should have had design review from the loaders team: it’s an entirely new way to import files, like an addition to `--require` and `--import` and `--loader`, and there has been no review of where it fits into the order of precedence relative to those other flags or whether the Loaders API should apply to it, for example. The changes introduced here and built on in #45916 amount to a new flow for importing files, that we need to coordinate with the Loaders API work and with refactors to module loading in general; for example, the Loaders API should presumably apply to files referenced by `--test` or `--test-reporter`, so that tests or reporters could be written in TypeScript, for example.

There is already an `--import` flag that can accept either a CommonJS or an ESM file or package. I would expect `--test` and `--test-reporter` to essentially be aliases of that, without needing any new modules infrastructure like `requireOrImport`. We should also discuss the expected outputs from these files; it seems like you’re expecting whatever `--test-reporter` points to to provide a default export that’s a function that’s the test reporter, but this means that the user is forced to declare the test reporter via this new flag. An alternative API that wouldn’t involve a few flag or import code path would be something like `import { registerTestReporter } from 'node:test'; registerTestReporter(testReporterFunction)`. Such an API would eliminate the need for changes to the modules system, I would think; a reporter could be written that used `registerTestReporter` to register itself, and the user could use it via `--import some-test-reporter` and it would work, even within `node_modules`. (This might not be your desired UX, which I completely understand, but we could discuss various options.)

In the near term, could the changes to `lib/internal/modules` from this PR please be reverted? Or this entire PR briefly reverted, if there’s no easy way to support test runners via an alternative API quickly. I support the new test runner and I think reporters would be a great feature, but the module loader is a delicate part of the codebase where there’s a lot in flight right now (see https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/45828, https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/45869, https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/44710). We need to coordinate a bit better going forward.

